80
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:45,540
Rayon!

81
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:48,780
Alright!

82
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,480
Nothing can stop us now!

83
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:51,560
Oh, man.

84
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:52,960
I can taste blood.

85
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,460
I hope he and it does not hurt too much.

86
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,280
But that block follow-up?

87
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:00,540
It's a good thing we have him out there right now.

88
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:05,420
He did that last time because he saw there was no choice but to have Asahi hit it.

89
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:11,180
Lately, Karasuno's style is to have everyone go up to attack, and those who don't become decoys.

90
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:15,360
They think more about not getting blocked than what to do if they actually are.

91
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:20,240
So when they do get blocked, it's more or less out of their hands.

92
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:25,040
Although when we were in middle school, we were constantly doing drills to make sure we always followed up.

93
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,020
If I was the coach, I'd do the same thing.

94
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:27,660
You know?

95
00:06:28,300 --> 00:06:31,040
You always want to know at least one person has your back.

96
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:32,980
