235
00:16:13,160 --> 00:16:14,160
Time!

236
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,160
What's the matter, Goshiki?

237
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,160
You've got to beat yourself up.

238
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,160
Remember, you're a talented player.

239
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:19,160
YAMAKUSHI!

240
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,160
Oh...

241
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,160
Thanks.

242
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:28,160
We'll stop the next one.

243
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,160
Right!

244
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:30,160
He doesn't lie or exaggerate.

245
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:31,160
Right!

246
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,160
And his words don't have any hidden meanings.

247
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,160
He just says it how it is.

248
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,160
From one ace to another.

249
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:40,160
They've turned it around!

250
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,160
That's three points in a row!

251
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:46,160
If they're able to keep this up, they might just pull off a miracle and win this thing!

252
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:47,160
Get it!

253
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:48,160
Get it, Karasuno!

254
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:58,160
Not bad!

255
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,160
Sweet!

256
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,160
That was perfect!

257
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,160
Did you see that?

258
00:17:09,160 --> 00:17:10,160
What a savage angle!

259
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:13,160
They snuck it through before they finished setting up the block.

260
00:17:17,160 --> 00:17:21,160
I bet that felt pretty good for him after his mistake with that last receive.

261
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,160
You did really good out there!

262
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,160
